      "nets": ["SCK"],
      "observed": "Net SCK connects U2 pin 3 (XTAL2/PB4) and U2 pin 7 (PB2), and U3 pin 3 (PB4) and U3 pin 7 (PB2), shorting two distinct I/O pins on each MCU.",
      "expected": "PB2 and PB4 should be on separate nets, as they are independent I/O pins (PB2 is SCK/SCL, PB4 is XTAL2/ADC2).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"12\") (name \"SCK\") ... (node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"3\") (pinfunction \"XTAL2/PB4\") (pintype \"bidirectional\")) (node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"7\") (pinfunction \"PB2\") (pintype \"bidirectional\")) (node (ref \"U3\") (pin \"3\") (pinfunction \"PB4\") (pintype \"bidirectional\")) (node (ref \"U3\") (pin \"7\") (pinfunction \"PB2\") (pintype \"bidirectional\"))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "Shorting PB2 and PB4 can cause I/O contention if either pin is driven as an output, and it merges the tach input, ISP SCK, and I2C SCL functions onto the same net, preventing proper operation of those interfaces.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["C2"],
      "pins": ["U1.2", "C2.1"],
      "nets": ["+5V"],
      "observed": "C2 is a 100nF capacitor on the +5V output of U1 (LM1117-5.0).",
      "expected": "The LM1117 datasheet requires a minimum 10µF output capacitor for stability; 100nF is insufficient.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"C2\") (value \"100nF\") ... (comp (ref \"U1\") (value \"LM1117-5.0\") (datasheet \"http://www.ti.com/lit/ds/symlink/lm1117.pdf\")"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The regulator may oscillate or be unstable, causing noise on the +5V rail and potential malfunction of the MCUs.",
      "confidence": 0.6
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design contains a clear bridged-net error shorting PB2 and PB4 on both ATtiny footprints, and a likely insufficient output capacitor on the LM1117 regulator."
}

